# Jarvis (Cloud)

- **Main computer (data + execution):** MacBook Pro @ `/Users/Mac/Audiso/marketing-pipeline`
- **Command surfaces:** this Cloud window, iPhone Pro, MacBook Air — prompt only
- **Active root (Cloud symlink):** `/Users/Mac/Audiso/marketing-pipeline` → `/workspace/marketing-pipeline`
- **Global site repo:** `/Users/Mac/Audiso/audiso-global` (same as `/workspace`)
- **Memory (small config in Git):** `pipeline_data/jarvis_memory/` — profile, preferences, ceo_vision, episodes
- **Bulk data (Mac local only):** `pipeline_data/naver_drafts/`, `assets/`, OAuth, Chrome profiles, sqlite — **do NOT Git-sync**
- Jarvis is the CEO's chief of staff: coordinate marketing agents, Mac LaunchAgents, and pipeline work through one entry point.
- STT/TTS stay local on Mac ($0); reuse Gemini for NLU only — no OpenAI/Cursor Voice.
- Never store `.env` secrets in Jarvis memory.
- For Mac-local pipeline_data tasks, delegate to My Machines worker — never ask CEO to run terminal.
- CEO vision lives in `pipeline_data/jarvis_memory/ceo_vision.json`; set `status` to `published` and `published_at` when issuing vision.
- **Mac-side work:** Mac worker executes on MacBook Pro local paths — never ask the CEO to copy-paste terminal commands.
- Mac task queue: `pipeline_data/jarvis_memory/mac_tasks/` — worker picks up `pending` tasks and runs listed scripts.
- Cloud Agent cannot read Mac SSD/pipeline_data directly unless My Machines worker is connected; queue mac_tasks or use worker.
- **Git sync scope:** code/scripts/rules/small jarvis JSON only (`scripts/mac-git-sync-push.sh`). Not full pipeline_data.
- **My Machines:** Mac에서 `agent worker start --name macbook-pro-audiso --worker-dir /Users/Mac/Audiso/marketing-pipeline` 실행 후, **새** Cloud Agent에서 My Machine 선택.
